{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508044-opinion-of-wod","id":1508044,"title":"Opinion of WOD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-11T09:22:44-07:00","id":1508044,"title":"Opinion of WOD","content":"Has anyone here heard an opinion on what an outsider thinks about the WOD, be it the whole thing or just a part of it, I've had some but I wanted to get a more general perspective if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T12:15:58-07:00","id":1508061,"title":"","content":"1) The vast majority of people have never heard of it, and have no opinions about it.<br /> <br /> 2) After that, is a very large group of people that basically think that the WoD was some old 90s thing that peaked in the early 2000s with the Bloodlines videogame and then faded away like many other 90s things; having no clue that products have been for the franchise in one form or another consistently for the past 20 years (they're not going to know that the &quot;new&quot; WoD is now the Chronicles of Darkness, and the older setting got revived and so on). A good portion of this crowd is vaguely aware that different companies have been trying to make a new VtM video game happen, but it's been a constant train wreck of cancelled AAA games and mediocre to bad smaller games. This only furthers the impression that the WoD is some 90s thing that belongs there.<br /> <br /> 3) Now we're starting to get into the blurry lines of when to count someone as an &quot;outsider&quot; or not, because we're getting into at least people that are very informed about the RPG hobby and have some historical perspective about it. Remember that there's plenty of people that play RPGs all the time and still fall into categories 1 or 2 because they just play the current/group favored edition of D&amp;D, or some clone of D&amp;D they like better. If we're considering &quot;outsider&quot; to mean, &quot;outside of the WoD fandom&quot; it also generates problems because these are going to be dominated by the reasons why they're not in the fandom, which can obfuscate their direct opinions of the games. There's also just way too many opinions here to generalize about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T23:58:20-07:00","id":1508119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508044-opinion-of-wod?p=1508061#post1508061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) After that, is a very large group of people that basically think that the WoD was some old 90s thing that peaked in the early 2000s with the Bloodlines videogame</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Vampire: the Masquerade - </i><i>Redemption</i> computer game also contributed to WoD's popularity and image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T00:07:02-07:00","id":1508121,"title":"","content":"Redemption is a bit more mixed in response... however it also came out years earlier, hence the idea that WoD peaked with Bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T07:17:17-07:00","id":1508152,"title":"","content":"If they've heard of it at all it consists of Vampire: the Masquerade. Maybe Hunter: the Vigil as well if they're in the wider RPG community. They probably don't know about the other game lines unless they've played a WoD/CofD game.<br /> <br /> Also WoD and CofD might as well be the same thing to many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T12:41:52-07:00","id":1508176,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the old Hunter the Reckoning video games we fairly popular, but didn't have the &quot;conversion&quot; rate of connecting fans of the video games to the wider WoD fandom. This isn't terribly shocking, the HtR video games are very much not what the RPG books play like, and those were already walled off a bit from the rest of the WoD as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:14:12-07:00","id":1508681,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness was an after-thought at White-Wolf until 2004. Games like Hunter's Hunted, Mafia and Gypsies are awesome, but, they require a rule book to play. For most players, that rule book was Vampire, and the players wanted to play vampires, not cool mafia-guys (well, one really liked gypsies). World of Darkness you kinda have to salvage and piece together from other White-Wolf game-lines. Even if you create a good, cool, World of Darkness setting, your players are always going to ask, &quot;So, where's the supernaturals, you know what I mean&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}